  "title": "Clint G NDE 4143",
  "date": "1986",
  "content": "When I was thirteen, I was shot in my right thigh with a rifle, the bullet broke my femoral artery vein in my leg. At the time I was shot, I had what seemed like a flash of my life, and all past experiences. Although I do not remember a single thing from this experience, I do know that it happened, the best way that I explained it over the years was like a giant picture of thousands on tiny pictures, that flashed in my mind. It was of course just a second or two, maybe more? As I awoke, getting up off the ground, I realized that I had been shot in the leg. I tried to stand up but could not I dropped back to the ground, as the blood started running down my leg. Immediately my leg ballooned out, from the clogging of the blood in my right thigh. Afterwards the doctors had told myself and my family, if this did not happen I would have bled to death within minutes. Since this time in my life, I became a free thinker, loner, not the same as what they would call the 'sheep' of society, definitely a very open minded person, with what many would call, and have over the years, strange and weird views on life. I also experienced since this time in my life twenty-three years ago, a sense of psychic abilities, it seems, a sense of having seen this before or thoughts in my head which would present themselves days later - much like enhanced déjà-vu.",
